Challenging Task 1
In this lab exercise, you will demonstrate the concept of Distributed Shared Memory (DSM) using two or more computers with different IP addresses.
One computer should create a shared variable (e.g., a number) and store it in a shared memory system accessible over the network.
A second computer should read the shared variable, modify its value (e.g., increment it), and write the updated value back to the shared storage.
The first computer should then read and display the updated value.
The task is considered complete when the changes made by one system are successfully reflected and visible on the other system(s), demonstrating shared access to common data in a distributed environment.
